./CHANGELOG.md:856:0.10.0 (2018-09-07)
./CHANGELOG.md:857:===================
./CHANGELOG.md:858:This is a new minor version release of ripgrep that contains some major new
./CHANGELOG.md:859:features, a huge number of bug fixes, and is the first release based on
./CHANGELOG.md:860:libripgrep. The entirety of ripgrep's core search and printing code has been
./CHANGELOG.md:861:rewritten and generalized so that anyone can make use of it.
./CHANGELOG.md:862:
./CHANGELOG.md:863:Major new features include PCRE2 support, multi-line search and a JSON output
./CHANGELOG.md:864:format.
./CHANGELOG.md:865:
./CHANGELOG.md:866:**BREAKING CHANGES**:
./CHANGELOG.md:867:
./CHANGELOG.md:868:* The minimum version required to compile Rust has now changed to track the
./CHANGELOG.md:869:  latest stable version of Rust. Patch releases will continue to compile with
./CHANGELOG.md:870:  the same version of Rust as the previous patch release, but new minor
./CHANGELOG.md:871:  versions will use the current stable version of the Rust compile as its
./CHANGELOG.md:872:  minimum supported version.
./CHANGELOG.md:873:* The match semantics of `-w/--word-regexp` have changed slightly. They used
./CHANGELOG.md:874:  to be `\b(?:<your pattern>)\b`, but now it's
./CHANGELOG.md:875:  `(?:^|\W)(?:<your pattern>)(?:$|\W)`. This matches the behavior of GNU grep
./CHANGELOG.md:876:  and is believed to be closer to the intended semantics of the flag. See
./CHANGELOG.md:877:  [#389](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/389) for more details.
./CHANGELOG.md:878:
./CHANGELOG.md:879:Feature enhancements:
./CHANGELOG.md:880:
./CHANGELOG.md:881:* [FEATURE #162](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/162):
./CHANGELOG.md:882:  libripgrep is now a thing. The primary crate is
./CHANGELOG.md:883:  [`grep`](https://docs.rs/grep).
./CHANGELOG.md:884:* [FEATURE #176](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/176):
./CHANGELOG.md:885:  Add `-U/--multiline` flag that permits matching over multiple lines.
./CHANGELOG.md:886:* [FEATURE #188](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/188):
./CHANGELOG.md:887:  Add `-P/--pcre2` flag that gives support for look-around and backreferences.
./CHANGELOG.md:888:* [FEATURE #244](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/244):
./CHANGELOG.md:889:  Add `--json` flag that prints results in a JSON Lines format.
./CHANGELOG.md:890:* [FEATURE #321](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/321):
./CHANGELOG.md:891:  Add `--one-file-system` flag to skip directories on different file systems.
./CHANGELOG.md:892:* [FEATURE #404](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/404):
./CHANGELOG.md:893:  Add `--sort` and `--sortr` flag for more sorting. Deprecate `--sort-files`.
./CHANGELOG.md:894:* [FEATURE #416](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/416):
./CHANGELOG.md:895:  Add `--crlf` flag to permit `$` to work with carriage returns on Windows.
./CHANGELOG.md:896:* [FEATURE #917](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/917):
./CHANGELOG.md:897:  The `--trim` flag strips prefix whitespace from all lines printed.
./CHANGELOG.md:898:* [FEATURE #993](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/993):
./CHANGELOG.md:899:  Add `--null-data` flag, which makes ripgrep use NUL as a line terminator.
./CHANGELOG.md:900:* [FEATURE #997](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/997):
./CHANGELOG.md:901:  The `--passthru` flag now works with the `--replace` flag.
./CHANGELOG.md:902:* [FEATURE #1038-1](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/1038):
./CHANGELOG.md:903:  Add `--line-buffered` and `--block-buffered` for forcing a buffer strategy.
./CHANGELOG.md:904:* [FEATURE #1038-2](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/1038):
./CHANGELOG.md:905:  Add `--pre-glob` for filtering files through the `--pre` flag.
