./CHANGELOG.md:1550:=====
./CHANGELOG.md:1551:This is a new minor version release of ripgrep that includes two breaking
./CHANGELOG.md:1552:changes with lots of bug fixes and some new features and performance
./CHANGELOG.md:1553:improvements. Notably, if you had a problem with colors or piping on Windows
./CHANGELOG.md:1554:before, then that should now be fixed in this release.
./CHANGELOG.md:1555:
./CHANGELOG.md:1556:**BREAKING CHANGES**:
./CHANGELOG.md:1557:
./CHANGELOG.md:1558:* ripgrep now requires Rust 1.11 to compile. Previously, it could build on
./CHANGELOG.md:1559:  Rust 1.9. The cause of this was the move from
./CHANGELOG.md:1560:  [Docopt to Clap](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/233)
./CHANGELOG.md:1561:  for argument parsing.
./CHANGELOG.md:1562:* The `-e/--regexp` flag can no longer accept a pattern starting with a `-`.
./CHANGELOG.md:1563:  There are two work-arounds: `rg -- -foo` and `rg [-]foo` or `rg -e [-]foo`
./CHANGELOG.md:1564:  will all search for the same `-foo` pattern. The cause of this was the move
./CHANGELOG.md:1565:  from [Docopt to Clap](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/233)
./CHANGELOG.md:1566:  for argument parsing.
./CHANGELOG.md:1567:  [This may get fixed in the
./CHANGELOG.md:1568:  future.](https://github.com/kbknapp/clap-rs/issues/742).
./CHANGELOG.md:1569:
./CHANGELOG.md:1570:Performance improvements:
./CHANGELOG.md:1571:
./CHANGELOG.md:1572:* [PERF #33](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/33):
./CHANGELOG.md:1573:  ripgrep now performs similar to GNU grep on small corpora.
./CHANGELOG.md:1574:* [PERF #136](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/136):
./CHANGELOG.md:1575:  ripgrep no longer slows down because of argument parsing when given a large
./CHANGELOG.md:1576:  argument list.
./CHANGELOG.md:1577:
./CHANGELOG.md:1578:Feature enhancements:
./CHANGELOG.md:1579:
./CHANGELOG.md:1580:* Added or improved file type filtering for Elixir.
./CHANGELOG.md:1581:* [FEATURE #7](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/7):
./CHANGELOG.md:1582:  Add a `-f/--file` flag that causes ripgrep to read patterns from a file.
./CHANGELOG.md:1583:* [FEATURE #51](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/51):
./CHANGELOG.md:1584:  Add a `--colors` flag that enables one to customize the colors used in
./CHANGELOG.md:1585:  ripgrep's output.
./CHANGELOG.md:1586:* [FEATURE #138](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/138):
./CHANGELOG.md:1587:  Add a `--files-without-match` flag that shows only file paths that contain
./CHANGELOG.md:1588:  zero matches.
./CHANGELOG.md:1589:* [FEATURE #230](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/230):
./CHANGELOG.md:1590:  Add completion files to the release (Bash, Fish and PowerShell).
./CHANGELOG.md:1591:
./CHANGELOG.md:1592:Bug fixes:
./CHANGELOG.md:1593:
./CHANGELOG.md:1594:* [BUG #37](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/37):
./CHANGELOG.md:1595:  Use correct ANSI escape sequences when `TERM=screen.linux`.
./CHANGELOG.md:1596:* [BUG #94](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/94):
./CHANGELOG.md:1597:  ripgrep now detects stdin on Windows automatically.
./CHANGELOG.md:1598:* [BUG #117](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/117):
