./CHANGELOG.md:1635:=====
./CHANGELOG.md:1636:Performance improvements:
./CHANGELOG.md:1637:
./CHANGELOG.md:1638:* [PERF #223](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/223):
./CHANGELOG.md:1639:  Added a parallel recursive directory iterator. This results in major
./CHANGELOG.md:1640:  performance improvements on large repositories.
./CHANGELOG.md:1641:* [PERF #11](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/pull/11):
./CHANGELOG.md:1642:  ripgrep now uses the `bytecount` library for counting new lines. In some
./CHANGELOG.md:1643:  cases, ripgrep runs twice as fast. Use
./CHANGELOG.md:1644:  `RUSTFLAGS="-C target-cpu=native" cargo build --release --features 'simd-accel avx-accel'`
./CHANGELOG.md:1645:  to get the fastest possible binary.
./CHANGELOG.md:1646:
./CHANGELOG.md:1647:Feature enhancements:
./CHANGELOG.md:1648:
./CHANGELOG.md:1649:* Added or improved file type filtering for Agda, Tex, Taskpaper, Markdown,
./CHANGELOG.md:1650:  asciidoc, textile, rdoc, org, creole, wiki, pod, C#, PDF, C, C++.
./CHANGELOG.md:1651:* [FEATURE #149](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/149):
./CHANGELOG.md:1652:  Add a new `--no-messages` flag that suppresses error messages.
./CHANGELOG.md:1653:  Note that `rg foo 2> /dev/null` also works.
./CHANGELOG.md:1654:* [FEATURE #159](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/159):
./CHANGELOG.md:1655:  Add a new `-m/--max-count` flag that limits the total number of matches
./CHANGELOG.md:1656:  printed for each file searched.
./CHANGELOG.md:1657:
./CHANGELOG.md:1658:Bug fixes:
